      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Implementation**\n\nI'm solidifying the implementation details. My priority is to create the `synthesize_ssml.py` file, incorporating Google Cloud Text-to-Speech as the designated provider. The code will explicitly reference and utilize Google's service.\n\n\n**Outlining the Structure**\n\nMy current focus is on structuring the `synthesize_ssml.py` file. I'm importing the `google.cloud.texttospeech` library to leverage Google's service. The architecture hinges on a function that ingests SSML, alongside voice and prosody parameters. This function will then use the Google Cloud Text-to-Speech client to synthesize the SSML. The provider's identity is cemented by the import and client instantiation.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789865649910,
          "start": 1789865647814
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc4e5ec6001p9NsiWMgiWfCBP",
